{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fermat_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fermat Problems\">2025 CEMC Fermat #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">2025 CEMC Cayley #11</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The current calendar year, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, is a perfect square. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> years from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, the calendar year will again be a perfect square. The smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2270de320e16349f510515506e38bb5706f78a10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2025 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 46 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"452\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we will need to use the next perfect square number. This will be subtracted from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dcabef99bd0dcab588d4e8e05801de9402298e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2025} = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4290728d2e7bd2036a0cefb7ec75110627dce53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{2} = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, the next perfect square number will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17fd14cf5e14e519cef139d514a8ea545c1c68c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(45 + 1)^{2} = 46^{2} = 2116$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the next perfect square year after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28236cde90fe8c0647e143503127f84fd5da255e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2116 - 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> years after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea58293a173162828ee90a641f5673a0990af05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use difference of squares to figure out the difference between the perfect squares, and use similar logic as solution 1to conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22ae70ca8a257f7f96bbcb742116c036e519d00e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025 = 45^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. This will also make it easier to find the difference without having to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154436c73c4d07565d1f75538e887ec19977139f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fa2b6fb13ed243dd708b722bc7628921c357de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(45 + 1)^{2} - 45^{2} = (45 + 1 - 45)(45 + 1 + 45) = 1 \\times 91 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 91}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"514\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>